        "original_id": "38bcd52b-1efc-5021-9cbb-1a28b259c4b7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eugene E. Lindsey\n- Ships: USS Nevada (BB-36), USS Saratoga (CV-3), USS Lexington (CV-2), USS Maryland (BB-46)\n- Organizations: bombing squadron, observation squadron\n- Topics: flight training, U.S. Navy service\n\nFacts:\n- Eugene E. Lindsey served on USS Nevada (BB-36) and USS Saratoga (CV-3) before completing flight training in 1929.\n- After completing flight training in 1929, Eugene E. Lindsey served with a bombing squadron in USS Lexington (CV-2).\n- After completing flight training in 1929, Eugene E. Lindsey served with an observation squadron in USS Maryland (BB-46).\n- USS Maryland (BB-46) was a Colorado-class battleship.\n- USS Maryland (BB-46) was also known to her crewmates as Old Mary and Fighting Mary.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
